<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mimnermus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 630 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mimnermus was a Greek elegiac poet from Colophon or Smyrna, active around 630 BCE. His surviving fragments lament the brevity of youth and the miseries of old age and celebrate love and pleasure. He also wrote on the history of Smyrna and its wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydians">Lydians</a>, and later poets regarded him as the founder of love elegy.</p></div>
